Here is the change specification to resolve the compiler warning and error based on the latest version of the `NimBLE-Arduino` library API:

### Change Specification for `src/ble_interface.cpp`

**1. Remove Deprecated Service Start and Start the Server Instead**
In newer versions of the `NimBLE-Arduino` library, calling `start()` on a specific service is deprecated because services are now started automatically when the main BLE Server starts. We need to remove `pService->start();` and instead call `pServer->start();`.

**2. Remove Invalid Scan Response Method**
The `setScanResponse(true)` method does not exist in the `NimBLEAdvertising` class (this was part of the older Bluedroid stack). NimBLE handles scan responses automatically when you add a service UUID to the advertising payload. We simply need to remove this line.

---

### Target File: `src/ble_interface.cpp`

**Remove:**
```cpp
    // Start the service
    pService->start();

    // Start advertising
    NimBLEAdvertising *pAdvertising = NimBLEDevice::getAdvertising();
    pAdvertising->addServiceUUID(SERVICE_UUID);
    pAdvertising->setScanResponse(true);
    pAdvertising->start();
```

**Replace With:**
```cpp
    // Start the server (this automatically starts all registered services)
    pServer->start();

    // Start advertising
    NimBLEAdvertising *pAdvertising = NimBLEDevice::getAdvertising();
    pAdvertising->addServiceUUID(SERVICE_UUID);
    // Note: NimBLE automatically handles scan response formatting internally
    pAdvertising->start();
```

