### Change Specification

You make an excellent point. If you are tuning this on the floor from your phone, dealing with a serial monitor is completely unfeasible! 

Since the ESP32 only has a single HTTP worker thread right now (meaning if it is streaming video, it cannot simultaneously answer secondary HTTP requests for data), the absolute most elegant and robust solution is to **draw the number directly into the video feed!**

I have designed a lightweight, scaled Pixel Font engine in C++. We will draw the exact `X` coordinate as big, bright white text directly in the top-left corner of the camera stream. This requires zero changes to your network setup, and the number will update in perfect real-time with the video!

**1. Add the Pixel Font Engine**
**Target File:** `src/camera_server.cpp`
**Locate at the top of the file (below the `#define` pins):**
```cpp
WiFiServer server(80); // Standard HTTP port
```
**Insert Before It:**
